From 6b493c37c09a942b5bf8e34e92873aa44f5b97c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: minhmc2007 <quangminh21072010@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 05:35:12 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] envsetup: do not enable ccache

  export USE_CCACHE=1

setup_ccache exports USE_CCACHE=1 and points CCACHE_EXEC at ccache on
every envsetup, so each build writes a cache whether or not one was
wanted. It also sets CCACHE_MAXSIZE itself, but a cache left at its
default is unbounded.

Commenting out the call rather than the body leaves USE_CCACHE unset, so
USE_CCACHE=1 in the environment still works, and re-enabling is deleting
one character.

Change-Id: If718cc565f46aaebdda7184fe12422e36237cd49
---
 envsetup.sh | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/envsetup.sh b/envsetup.sh
index db06cb6..2bdc2ec 100644
--- a/envsetup.sh
+++ b/envsetup.sh
@@ -3496,7 +3496,8 @@ function skipGlobs() {
 }
 
 setup_keys
-setup_ccache
+# ccache off, it defaults USE_CCACHE=1 and grows without bound.
+#setup_ccache
 validate_current_shell
 set_global_paths
 source_vendorsetup
-- 
2.55.0

